test.sh
test.conf
# Exception to the test.sh rule above: PRIDE-PPPAR's own vendored install.sh
# (addons/PRIDE-PPPAR/install.sh) requires example/test.sh to exist (it globs
# `./example/*.sh` unconditionally, before the non-interactive "run tests?"
# prompt is even answered) - this is the upstream test harness entry point,
# not this project's own test.sh convention the blanket rule above targets.
!/addons/PRIDE-PPPAR/example/test.sh
*.FCStd1
**/venv*/*
**/build/
/rtkbase